.TH VALIDIP 1 "2026-04-14" "validip 1.2.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
validip \- validate IPv4 and IPv6 address format
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B validip
[\fB\-h\fR | \fB\-\-help\fR]
[\fB\-V\fR | \fB\-\-version\fR]
.I ip_address
.PP
.B source validip
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B validip
is a Bash utility that validates IPv4 and IPv6 address formats. In script
mode it accepts a single IP address as a positional argument; the address
family is auto-detected by the presence of a colon (IPv6) or a period
(IPv4).
.PP
When sourced as a Bash module,
.B validip
exports three functions:
.BR valid_ip ", " valid_ip4 ", and " valid_ip6 .
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Display help and exit.
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Display version and exit.
.TP
.B \-\-
End-of-options sentinel. Subsequent arguments are treated as positional
even if they begin with a dash.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Valid IP address.
.TP
.B 1
Invalid IP address.
.TP
.B 22
Missing argument, unknown option, or too many arguments (EINVAL).
.SH VALIDATION RULES
.SS IPv4
Four decimal octets separated by periods, each in the range 0\-255.
Leading zeros are rejected (for example
.IR 010.0.0.1
is invalid), matching
.BR inet_pton (3)
behaviour.
.SS IPv6
Standard eight-hextet form, zero-compression
.RB ( :: ),
IPv4-mapped
.RB ( ::ffff:1.2.3.4 ),
IPv4-embedded in the last 32 bits
.RB ( 2001:db8::1.2.3.4 ),
and zone identifiers
.RB ( fe80::1%eth0 ).
Addresses with three or more consecutive colons or multiple
.B ::
zero-compression sequences are rejected.
.SH EXPORTED FUNCTIONS
When sourced, the following functions become available in the caller's
shell (marked with
.BR "declare -fx" ):
.TP
.BI "valid_ip " ip
Dispatches to
.B valid_ip4
or
.B valid_ip6
based on the presence of a colon. Returns 0 if valid, 1 otherwise.
.TP
.BI "valid_ip4 " ip
Validate an IPv4 address. Returns 0 on success, 1 on failure.
.TP
.BI "valid_ip6 " ip
Validate an IPv6 address. Returns 0 on success, 1 on failure.
.SH EXAMPLES
Validate from a shell prompt:
.PP
.EX
validip 192.168.1.1 && echo valid
validip ::1 && echo valid
validip ::ffff:192.168.1.1 && echo valid
validip fe80::1%eth0 && echo valid
.EE
.PP
Use as a module inside a script:
.PP
.EX
source validip
if valid_ip "$ip"; then
  echo "Valid IPv4 or IPv6"
fi
.EE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR internetip (1),
.BR watchip (1),
.BR inet_pton (3)
.SH AUTHOR
Biksu Okusi <biksu@okusi.id>
